# Commit Reminders

After completing any of the following, remind the user to commit before moving on:

- A feature or component is working and verified on device
- A build error is fixed and the build is green
- A cleanup or refactor session ends
- Any `*_gen.c` file is manually edited (CLI will overwrite it on next `lved-cli generate`)
- The image asset pipeline is run (`gen_image_data_lvgl.ps1`)
- `globals.xml` or any XML is changed and `lved-cli` is about to be run

## Why it matters for this project

- `lved-cli.js generate ui` overwrites all `*_gen.*` files from XML — any hand edits in those files are lost without a prior commit
- `soc_gauge_gen.c` and `speedometer_gen.c` contain significant hand-written logic that lives in `*_gen.*` files and will be wiped by the CLI
- The session summary only captures the previous session — changes made in the current session are not recoverable from AI memory

## Reminder wording

Keep it short, e.g.:
> "Good time to commit before we move on — want me to do it?"
